    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense for general behavior, but the staff needs more specific visual cues to help with the initial \"vibe check\" when guests first arrive in the lobby. Since we are in Dubai, we see a huge variety of people. Specifically, when looking at guest demographics, are there certain cultural markers or styles of dress that typically correlate with guests who might be more prone to causing public disturbances or who might lack the \"refined\" etiquette our VIPs expect? Like, are there specific groups or types of attire that usually flag as a higher risk for social friction in a high-end setting?",
